{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"records\": [\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D121-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"a2b88e63d2b89461a879c84d1b0cce3ee7654c9205aa63403d29e91c2d0b79c2\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 recruits concealment; A3 withholds the envelope's purpose and risk.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 evades B2's contents question; A5 answers B4's involvement concern.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B4 worries about involvement, but A5's reassurance changes no practical terms.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 introduces 'promotion' without increasing B4's concrete responsibility.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies an envelope, hamper and imminent arrivals, though no relationship.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'hamper level' neatly minimizes complicity; 'promotion' is more ornamental.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 80\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Hide this envelope under the picnic hamper before Mum comes in.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"She asked me to unpack the hamper.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then keep the envelope in your pocket while you unpack.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll end up taking it home.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Perfect. I'll explain when she stops asking where it is.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A recruits practical help concealing a secret while postponing disclosure of what helping entails.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Delegating evidence handling could look similar, but D121 specifically depends on withholding risk or purpose.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 makes explanation conditional on concealment; revised A5 postpones explanation until Mum stops asking.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative turns B's helpful logistics into wider concealment; alternative b bargains over a custodian's conditions.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Replaced the vague promotion with an accidental extension of custody, introducing Mum as the approaching person. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5 (A5 delays disclosure), logic 5 (A3 uses unpacking; A5 uses taking it home), relationship 4 (B2 has a task), heightening 4 (A5 extends concealment), specificity 4 (A1 establishes family packing), brevity/wit 4 (A5 sincerely welcomes the complication): 90/100. Five spoken turns and 54 words; internal pass only.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The envelope remains deliberately unexplained; performance must make A's relief sincere rather than knowingly sinister.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D121-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"7866f2dbe87ee4e3adc80bf8a187c16eef6878b5dede14d1d45466d5b1633f54\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 asks B to hold the key and remain silent; A3 never reveals the purpose.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 gives a circular answer to B2; A5 echoes B4's curiosity without managing it.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"B2 asks 'Why?' and B4 reports curiosity but sets no meaningful condition.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5's pocket metaphor merely repeats A1's request for storage and silence.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 identifies a cupboard key and tomorrow, but leaves the situation unlocated.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5's curiosity-in-pocket image is compact but substitutes wordplay for a new tactic.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 65\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Keep the spare cupboard key till tomorrow. Don't tell your flatmate I've left it here.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Only if you tell me what's in the cupboard.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Could you accept knowing what isn't? Nothing alive.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Then you collect it before she gets home.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Agreed. Text me when she leaves work. Just 'key', please.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A secures another person's silence and custody while offering less information than an informed helper would want.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"A cover story seeks endorsement of an explanation; this card seeks assistance before an explanation is supplied.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A1 requests secrecy about the key; revised A3 offers only 'Nothing alive' instead of the contents.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Unlike a's opportunistic extension of concealment, b uses limited disclosure and a negotiated collection deadline.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Rebuilt the exchange around a flatmate and conditional cooperation. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 limits disclosure), logic 5 (A3 answers B2's demand; A5 accepts B4's deadline), relationship 4 (B2 and B4 set terms), heightening 4 (A5 adds coded coordination), specificity 4 (A1 establishes shared housing), brevity/wit 4 (A3's narrow reassurance serves persuasion): 90/100. Five spoken turns, under 75 words; internal pass only.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The 'Nothing alive' reassurance is familiar comic territory, though it serves A's precise information bargain.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D122-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"ccaf84ff0e76886f28a0ec45bd1575479c3534b91789b0c2b4b6e8f277576383\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 and A5 delay departure for an explanation, but the receipt's contradiction is unclear.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 rejects B2's postponement; A5 asks for the destination of B4's detour.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 wants to defer the discussion, but B4 offers little beyond 'a detour'.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 narrows the question but does not materially develop the ten-minute pressure in A3.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1's 'missing hour on this receipt' does not establish what account is suspicious.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 and A5 favor balanced phrases about hours and destinations over plain pursuit.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 68\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Before you catch that bus: you said you left work at six. Why's your taxi receipt timed five?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll explain tomorrow. That's the last bus.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll drive you. What happened to that hour?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I left early to collect your birthday present.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Lovely. Explain why you needed a taxi home from my sister's before we go.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A makes departure conditional on explaining one suspicious discrepancy and removes reasons to postpone.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"General truth investigation compares evidence; D122 makes keeping this person present the immediate tactic.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A1 frames questioning around the bus; revised A3 offers transport so B cannot defer the missing-hour explanation.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a removes a practical obstacle by offering a lift; b uses a booking that B needs A to complete.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Clarified the receipt discrepancy and introduced birthday concealment as B's explanation. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 and A5 postpone departure), logic 5 (A3 solves B2's bus problem; A5 challenges B4's explanation), relationship 4 (B has transport and surprise concerns), heightening 4 (A5 tests the detour's endpoint), specificity 4 (A1 gives conflicting times), brevity/wit 4 (A3's helpful lift prolongs questioning): 90/100. Five spoken turns, 74 words; internal pass only.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 introduces the sister's address late; it must play as another detail on the same receipt, not an unrelated accusation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D122-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"e2f511c2ef9c0dc5ef648ce2d0a6155799a1435ec06fee3cbfa969e05f191baf\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 explicitly blocks leaving, but A5 shifts from the changed date to the unchanged name.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 counters B2's departure; A5 uses B4's booking change to ask about responsibility.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 needs to leave, but neither that need nor the booking's relationship is developed.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 adds personal stakes through 'my name' but leaves the original date question unresolved.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 gives Friday and Monday; B4 supplies a booking without identifying its purpose.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's Monday-versus-Friday personification is brief and connected to A1's discrepancy.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 72\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Wait before you go. You said our wedding venue was booked for Friday. This says Monday.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Monday was cheaper. Can you sign? I'm late for work.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Stay while I read it. You told me Friday was confirmed.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It was. I moved it after we sent the invitations.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then work needs to wait. Explain when you planned to tell the Friday guests.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A holds B in a conversation until B accounts for a suspicious change in an established story.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Demanding an apology addresses the harm of concealment; this card first requires an account before departure.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 says 'Not until'; revised A3 and A5 explicitly require B to stay and explain the date change.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The wedding signature gives b shared logistical stakes and leverage; a instead offers assistance to keep the question alive.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Made the changed booking a wedding venue and kept every question on the date change. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 and A5 keep B present), logic 5 (A3 uses the signature request; A5 uses already-sent invitations), relationship 4 (B wants savings and a signature), heightening 4 (A5 brings guests into the same discrepancy), specificity 5 (A1 establishes a wedding date), brevity/wit 3 (A5 is playable but more tense than comic): 90/100. Five spoken turns, under 75 words; internal pass only.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The scenario carries substantial relational tension and offers less comic lightness than the transport alternative.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D123-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"27fcd178317705ff61f29034fc102b6942946e1be04fda5fc06e526fdc472ea0\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 separates cancellation from concealment; A5 demands acknowledgment of not knowing.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 rebuts B2's wish not to upset A with the cake arrival; A5 corrects B4's misplaced apology.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 claims protective intent and B4 attempts repair, giving A two distinct responses to address.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 rejects the offered apology's object and specifies the unacknowledged harm.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes an undisclosed cancellation; A3's arrival with a cake makes its cost immediately playable.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'Try the part where I didn't know' economically exposes B4's evasive apology.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 94\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'm not asking you to apologise for cancelling. Apologise for not telling me.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I didn't want to upset you.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"So you let me arrive with a cake instead.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'm sorry the party didn't happen.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Try the part where I didn't know.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A insists that B acknowledge the harm caused by concealment separately from the underlying cancellation.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Seeking a generic apology could accept regret about the party; D123 requires acknowledgment of the withheld information.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 explicitly exempts cancellation, and A5 redirects B4's apology to A's ignorance.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a corrects a misdirected apology after social embarrassment; b seeks recognition of consent denied by selective disclosure.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained exactly: B2 causes the concrete rebuttal in A3, and B4's attempted repair causes A5's sharper specification. Internal rereview confirms the original dimension scores and 94/100; all five spoken-turn gates pass. No improvement or independent testing is claimed.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A1 states the distinction unusually explicitly, but the cake and failed apology dramatize it instead of merely repeating it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D123-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"fb51ed5d6b20364466725ef5fd26053d138022e40d1b35423c2c0395fe97e6c3\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 identifies a withheld refusal-triggering fact; A5 requests acknowledgment of the lost choice.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 challenges B2's 'important facts'; A5 turns B4's helping claim toward prevented choice.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B4 asserts helpful intent, but the actual benefit and relationship remain unspecified.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 reframes A3's changed answer as lost choice without adding concrete consequence.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies half a letter but never identifies the decision or omitted fact.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5's abstract 'prevented me from choosing' sounds more like an argument summary than speech.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 74\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You showed me the rescue dog's photo, not the page saying he eats sofas.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"He needed a home.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I understand. Admit that hiding the sofa page changed my yes.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll buy you another sofa.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Thank you. Before we feed him another one, say I should have had both pages.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A seeks acknowledgment that selective disclosure deprived A of a meaningful choice, even when B's motive was defensible.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Compensation for damage could settle the practical loss without acknowledging the misdirection that produced consent.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A5 names prevented choice; revised A5 accepts the sofa offer while still requiring acknowledgment of both pages.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Unlike a's evasive verbal apology, b gives B a concrete repair offer that A appreciates but finds insufficient.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Introduced a rescue-dog adoption and an omitted behavior page to embody the withheld fact. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 separates motive from concealment), logic 5 (A3 accepts B2's motive; A5 uses B4's sofa offer), relationship 4 (B wants the dog housed and offers repair), heightening 4 (A5 insists on acknowledgment despite compensation), specificity 5 (A1 names the omission), brevity/wit 4 (A5's next sofa follows the dog's behavior): 92/100. Five spoken turns, under 75 words; internal pass only.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The sofa-eating exaggeration should remain an ordinary household complaint so the acknowledgment request retains emotional weight.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D124-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"873025a169007780a9e6c4bbac3c7559f359be1db3ddea1a4930195ac3276ad8\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 requests agreement on an innocent explanation; A5 seeks agreement that the key served chair collection.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 incorporates B2's cupboard opening; A5 supplies a protective account for B4's key.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 corrects the account and B4 anticipates scrutiny, acting as a cautious implicated partner.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 extends A3's furniture emphasis to explain away the incriminating key.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes chair collection and a locked cupboard, though the protected stakes stay implicit.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'Between chairs' and A5's practical-tool claim arise from the same protective explanation.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"We were collecting chairs, not investigating the locked cupboard. Agreed?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We did open the cupboard.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Between chairs. Let's emphasise the furniture.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"What if they ask about the key?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"We can agree it was a very practical chair-collecting tool.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A obtains B's endorsement of an innocent explanation by incorporating inconvenient facts into it.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Rehearsing a shared witness account emphasizes remembering and defending events; D124 centers assent to a protective explanation.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 asks 'Agreed?' and A5 again seeks agreement on what the key was for.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a negotiates a cover with an implicated collaborator; revised b asks a supervisor to endorse wording that protects a volunteer.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained exactly: B2 makes A3 qualify the chair account, and B4 requires A5 to explain the key within it. Internal rereview confirms the original dimension scores and 90/100. The five spoken turns sustain the same protective explanation without a forced outcome.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The cupboard's significance and consequences of discovery remain implicit; the scene relies on shared impropriety being playable.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D124-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"cc6f258705a02636281f0954fe9ca68d6a348e0854ba4505463546512ec2caac\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 explicitly asks B to back the traffic explanation, but the protected plan or person is unspecified.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 converts B2's parking into stationary traffic; A5 incorporates B4's bakery location.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 expose facts but express no stake in endorsing or refusing the explanation.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 stretches the traffic account to cakes without increasing the demand for endorsement.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1's missing hour and B4's bakery locate an incident but not its audience or consequences.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'Stationary traffic' is compact; A5's cake bottleneck risks becoming a detachable gag.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 69\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Can you approve 'delivery delay' in the newsletter? I don't want our new volunteer blamed for the melted cake.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"She delivered it on time. We left it by the radiator.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then 'storage problem'. Will you approve that?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Only if we mention the refund.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Absolutely. 'Storage problem; full refund arranged.' Can I put your name under it?\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A negotiates an endorsed public explanation that protects an involved person's reputation.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Merely inventing an excuse does not satisfy the card unless A pursues another person's endorsement.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A1 asks B to back an explanation; revised A3 asks approval and A5 requests B's name beneath it.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b uses a cooperative approval bargain and financial remedy; a uses collusive reinterpretation of a key and cupboard.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Introduced a newsletter, volunteer and melted cake to establish whom the account protects. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5 (A1 names protection; A5 seeks endorsement), logic 5 (A3 corrects the delivery claim; A5 incorporates B4's refund), relationship 5 (B corrects facts and imposes accountability), heightening 4 (A5 requests named backing), specificity 5 (A1 establishes publication stakes), brevity/wit 3 (the negotiated wording is lightly comic): 93/100. Five spoken turns, under 75 words; internal pass only.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The final explanation is defensible and restrained, so its comic effect depends on A's investment in securing the signature.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D125-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"08e4b00393cffa137ea3a652c1dcac4e451a83edb685f9b9efddc0fd507cf7b8\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 transfers custody of the labelled box; A5 narrows the language of responsibility without taking it back.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's label objection as a reason for moving the box; A5 answers B4's responsibility objection.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 identifies traceability and B4 names the burden, requiring A to justify the transfer.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 reveals anticipated searching; A5 persists by redefining the resulting responsibility as storage.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 gives a labelled box, cupboard and calls; A3 supplies the reason A cannot retain it.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'job description' makes A's evasive division of labor concise and playable.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 86\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Keep this labelled box in your cupboard. I'll handle the calls.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Your name's on the label.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Exactly. Mine is the first cupboard they'll check.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You're making me responsible.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"For storage. Let's keep the job description reassuringly narrow.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A shifts responsibility for a troublesome physical loose end to B while minimizing the apparent scope of the job.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Recruiting secrecy before disclosure resembles this scene, but D125's central objective is offloading custody and responsibility.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 divides storage from calls; B4 explicitly names responsibility, which A5 keeps assigned to B.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a transfers a physical object despite resistance; b delegates an explanation and supplies language when B cooperates.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained exactly: B2's name-label objection becomes A3's reason to move the box, and B4's burden objection produces A5's narrower job description. Internal rereview confirms the original dimension scores and 86/100; five spoken turns and causal links pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 heightens by entrenching 