dition A's later commitment on B's result; here B is assigned the actual follow-up.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 gives B the treasurer conversation outright, and A5 supplies its opening without offering to take over later.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Unlike a's continued resistance to physical custody, b allows B's practical cooperation to become A's next delegation tactic.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained exactly: B2 generates A3's neutrality rationale, while B4's helpful question causes A5 to supply an opening and reinforce B's suitability. Internal rereview confirms the original dimension scores and 90/100; the spoken ABABA exchange passes the gates.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The treasurer relationship is clear, but the receipt's amount and consequences remain unspecified; a longer scene would need discovery.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D126-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"c247a20c31ba06a37e47c1e877520789f02554650439e88efc7d882ae745d951\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 compares conflicting labels and A3 asks for observable detail, but A5 does not test the new lid evidence.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 responds to B2's uncertainty; A5's generic 'build the object' barely uses B4's rigid lid.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2's uncertainty and B4's extra detail support inquiry, but B has no stated practical concern.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 announces a method instead of advancing a concrete consistency test prompted by B4.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's bag-or-box discrepancy and A3's handles are tangible, immediately playable details.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's noun line is pointed, but A5 ends in an abstract investigative maxim.\"}\n        },\n        